  "body": "## What changed\n\nFollow-up to #696: the same #579/#583 clash also broke `probe_dialects`, which failed 3 of 13 on main (Haas, Mazak and Sinumerik bore centre). #696 only covered the Tormach goldens.\n\n- **Regenerated goldens:** `golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/probe_bore_centre.nc`.\n  - **Stale:** a rapid to Z25 over the part.\n  - **Now (main's output):** a rapid only to the Z50 safe plane, then a protected positioning move down to Z25 with its hit check (`G31` on Haas and Mazak, `MEAS=1` on Sinumerik), as #570 requires.\n- **Checked by reading:** no rapid below the safe plane remains in any of the three.\n- **`probe_dialects.rs`:** Mazak's first no-contact `GOTO` label moves from 9002 to 9003, because one more guard now runs ahead of it. The comment says so.\n\n## Pinned by\n\n`probe_dialects`: `haas_bore_centre_posts_g31_skips`, `mazak_bore_centre_posts_g31_skips_with_goto_tests`, `sinumerik_bore_centre_posts_meas_blocks`.\n\n## How tested\n\n`probe_dialects` (13/13), `probe_tormach` (7/7), `probe_guard` (5/5) and `probe_op` (12/12) pass on upstream main 4aec95a9 (with #696 merged) plus this commit.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nOther suites: no other suite reads these goldens. The branch is cut from upstream/main. The fork is synced at v0.16.0.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #695\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
